1.2. src/engine/runtime/stepGameSimulation.ts — Resolver $self / $other y Física 2D con Hijos (parentId)
En executeActionList, añade el parámetro opcional ctx?: { owner?: GameObjectData; other?: GameObjectData } y resuelve un helper resolveActionTarget(ref):
Ts
function resolveActionTarget(
  rawRef: unknown,
  objectMap: Map<string, GameObjectData>,
  ctx?: { owner?: GameObjectData; other?: GameObjectData }
): GameObjectData | undefined {
  const ref = String(rawRef ?? '').trim();
  if (!ref) return ctx?.owner;
  if (ref === '$self') return ctx?.owner;
  if (ref === '$other') return ctx?.other;
  const direct = objectMap.get(ref);
  if (direct) return direct;
  for (const obj of objectMap.values()) {
    if (obj.name === ref) return obj;
  }
  return undefined;
}
Y al disparar reglas de colisión/trigger en el bucle de mechanics, guarda (matchedOwner, matchedOther) y pásalos a executeActionList(mech.actions, mech.id, state, objectMap, { owner: matchedOwner, other: matchedOther }).
En resolveAxisHorizontal y resolveAxisVertical, si obj.parentId existe, convierte el desplazamiento mundial al espacio local del padre usando stageDeltaToParentLocal de ../core/math:
Ts
import { getWorldTransform, stageDeltaToParentLocal } from '../core/math';

function applyWorldDeltaToObject(
  obj: GameObjectData,
  dxWorld: number,
  dyWorld: number,
  objectMap: Map<string, GameObjectData>
): void {
  if (!obj.parentId) {
    obj.transform.x += dxWorld;
    obj.transform.y += dyWorld;
    return;
  }
  const local = stageDeltaToParentLocal(dxWorld, dyWorld, obj.parentId, objectMap);
  obj.transform.x += local.x;
  obj.transform.y += local.y;
}
